  "analysis": "Both responses outline a multi‑lane plan with gates, reviewers, and rollback steps, but VVD directly addresses the hard single‑writer limit by provisioning separate cache volumes, includes concrete cost‑window timing, and provides a safe fallback that avoids the irreversible database rollback. NLG suggests sharding to temporary directories and a final merge on the same volume, which may still hit the hardware bottleneck and relies on a risky DB rollback path. VVD therefore offers a more realistic, complete solution with fewer likely follow‑up questions.",
